Both steps use the SObject Collections resource (`/composite/sobjects`).

**Step 1 — atomic insert:** a single `POST` with `allOrNone: true` creates all three contacts in one transaction. If any record fails validation (e.g., a duplicate email rule), none of the three is created.

**Step 2 — partial-success update:** a single `PATCH` with `allOrNone: false` lets each record in the batch succeed or fail independently, and mixed object types (Account + Opportunity) are allowed in one collection request. The response reports a per-record result, so one failure won't block the other save. (Using the collection endpoint here also keeps the bulk pattern intact if more records are added later.)

